# Team workflow (always applies)

**Read and follow `AGENTS.md` at the repo root. It is the single source of truth.** @AGENTS.md

Non-negotiables (details in AGENTS.md):

- Never commit or push to `main`. Start every task with:
  `git checkout main && git pull --ff-only && git checkout -b <name>/<short-desc>`
  (e.g. `sai/genie-dashboard`: the human's first name, 2-4 kebab words).
- Stay within the task's scope. One branch = one PR.
- Commit messages: Conventional Commits (`feat(scope): ...`, `fix: ...`, `feat!: ...` for breaking) with a body for the next agent: why, approach, gotchas, how verified, follow-ups. As long as needed, no padding.
- Tests: required for new logic, every bug fix (regression test), and data-pipeline changes (data checks). Run lint + tests before pushing. Never delete or weaken a test silently.
- Add a user-facing line under `## [Unreleased]` in `CHANGELOG.md` (Keep a Changelog sections: Added / Changed / Deprecated / Removed / Fixed / Security).
- Never choose a version number by hand; run `scripts/next-version.sh`.
- Push the feature branch, open a PR whose title is a Conventional Commit header, fill `.github/pull_request_template.md`, then report the link and stop.
- Never merge, tag, force-push, delete branches, add dependencies, or spend cloud money without explicit human approval.
- Append new gotchas/decisions as dated lines to AGENTS.md §12 / §13.
